1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,893
On its own, an AI model only knows what it learned in general.

2
00:00:04,893 --> 00:00:09,186
This video shows how to give an assistant your own knowledge, so that

3
00:00:09,186 --> 00:00:13,480
it answers from your documents and shows where each answer came from.

4
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:22,211
A general model does not know your prices, your policies or your help

5
00:00:22,211 --> 00:00:25,570
articles, so it guesses, or says that it does not know.

6
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:27,915
Knowledge fixes that.

7
00:00:27,915 --> 00:00:33,230
The assistant looks up the passages that match each question, and answers from them.

8
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:38,328
For content such as the pages of a site, the answer carries small

9
00:00:38,328 --> 00:00:42,186
numbers, and a numbered list of sources appears under it.

10
00:00:42,186 --> 00:00:45,860
Documents on a profile work quietly in the background.

11
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:51,315
Your content is kept in a search index that understands meaning, not only

12
00:00:51,315 --> 00:00:56,140
words, so a question finds the right passage even when the wording differs.

13
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:03,518
A few files, such as a price list or a policy:

14
00:01:03,518 --> 00:01:05,718
upload documents to a profile.

15
00:01:05,718 --> 00:01:09,080
You keep them current by uploading a new version.

16
00:01:09,830 --> 00:01:12,851
Files a person wants to ask about in one chat:

17
00:01:12,851 --> 00:01:14,768
let the person attach them.

18
00:01:14,768 --> 00:01:16,860
They belong to that chat only.

19
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:22,665
Large or changing content, such as the articles or products of a site:

20
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:25,990
a data source, which the site keeps in step.

21
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:29,663
A folder of files, or a public website:

22
00:01:29,663 --> 00:01:34,080
a file source or a web crawler, which read them on a schedule.

23
00:01:38,289 --> 00:01:40,940
Documents need a search index.

24
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:47,789
Open Search, Indexes, click Add index, and click Add on AI Documents for Elasticsearch.

25
00:01:48,256 --> 00:01:50,549
Enter an Index Name and a Name.

26
00:01:50,549 --> 00:01:57,612
Documents are embedded with the site's default embedding deployment, which you choose in the default models.

27
00:01:57,612 --> 00:02:00,276
Click Save, and the index is created.

28
00:02:00,734 --> 00:02:05,681
Then open Settings, Artificial Intelligence, and find the Documents section.

29
00:02:05,681 --> 00:02:08,276
Choose the index under Index profile.

30
00:02:08,276 --> 00:02:13,284
It holds the documents of profiles and the files that people attach to chats.

31
00:02:13,772 --> 00:02:18,752
Avoid switching to another index once people use it, because the documents stored

32
00:02:18,752 --> 00:02:21,099
in the old one are no longer found.

33
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,072
Click Save.

34
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:32,156
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, edit the profile, and open the Knowledge tab.

35
00:02:32,156 --> 00:02:38,043
Documents on a profile are background knowledge that the assistant uses in every chat.

36
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:45,310
Drag files onto the upload area, or click Browse Files.

37
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:47,347
Here is a return policy.

38
00:02:47,347 --> 00:02:49,996
A new file shows a Pending badge.

39
00:02:52,145 --> 00:02:57,853
Document Top N is how many matching passages the assistant reads for each question.

40
00:02:57,853 --> 00:03:02,535
More passages give more context, but cost more and slow the answer.

41
00:03:03,077 --> 00:03:06,873
Document retrieval mode decides what the assistant gets.

42
00:03:06,873 --> 00:03:09,628
Chunk gives only the matching passages.

43
00:03:09,628 --> 00:03:15,077
Hierarchical gives the whole documents they come from, which suits short documents.

44
00:03:15,649 --> 00:03:16,775
Click Save.

45
00:03:16,775 --> 00:03:20,486
The file is read, split into passages and indexed.

46
00:03:20,486 --> 00:03:24,529
The supported formats are listed under the upload area.

47
00:03:28,732 --> 00:03:30,852
Now ask the assistant.

48
00:03:30,852 --> 00:03:35,622
In the list of profiles, open Actions and click New chat.

49
00:03:36,075 --> 00:03:40,569
Ask something that only the document can answer, such as within how many

50
00:03:40,569 --> 00:03:43,565
business days Contoso refunds a returned item.

51
00:03:44,038 --> 00:03:46,949
The assistant answers from the document:

52
00:03:46,949 --> 00:03:51,378
the refund takes five business days, exactly as the policy says.

53
00:03:51,834 --> 00:03:57,448
Documents on a profile work quietly in the background, so the answer has no source list.

54
00:03:57,448 --> 00:04:02,584
Data sources, which show numbered sources under an answer, have their own video.

55
00:04:06,884 --> 00:04:11,502
To let people attach files to a chat, tick Allow session document uploads

56
00:04:11,502 --> 00:04:13,080
on the Knowledge tab.

57
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:18,164
Allow session image uploads adds pictures, and needs a default vision deployment.

58
00:04:18,642 --> 00:04:23,771
Largest document that can be indexed is the longest document, in characters of

59
00:04:23,771 --> 00:04:26,030
text, that a person can attach.

60
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:29,082
A bigger one is refused when it is attached.

61
00:04:29,546 --> 00:04:35,301
Describe figures in uploaded documents decides whether the AI describes the charts and

62
00:04:35,301 --> 00:04:37,866
pictures inside attached documents.

63
00:04:37,866 --> 00:04:40,806
It uses a vision model, so it costs more.

64
00:04:41,284 --> 00:04:44,134
Attached files belong to one chat only.

65
00:04:44,134 --> 00:04:47,934
They never become part of the profile's own knowledge.

66
00:04:52,134 --> 00:04:56,124
A data source connects the assistant to a knowledge base built from a

67
00:04:56,124 --> 00:04:59,954
search index or a database, such as all the articles of your site.

68
00:05:00,704 --> 00:05:04,825
A file source reads a folder of files on a schedule, from the

69
00:05:04,825 --> 00:05:06,670
site's server, an F.T.P.

70
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:08,207
site or an S.F.T.P.

71
00:05:08,207 --> 00:05:08,884
site.

72
00:05:09,634 --> 00:05:13,966
A web crawler reads a public website page by page, and the sources

73
00:05:13,966 --> 00:05:16,854
in answers link back to the original page.

74
00:05:17,604 --> 00:05:23,227
A documentation search tool instance searches a public documentation site live, only when

75
00:05:23,227 --> 00:05:24,944
the assistant needs it.

76
00:05:29,144 --> 00:05:35,184
With preemptive retrieval on, in the Default Orchestrator settings, the assistant searches your

77
00:05:35,184 --> 00:05:37,336
knowledge before every answer.

78
00:05:37,336 --> 00:05:41,164
With it off, it searches when it decides that it needs to.

79
00:05:41,914 --> 00:05:47,130
Restrict answers to retrieved data only keeps the assistant to your content.

80
00:05:47,130 --> 00:05:52,474
When nothing matches, it says so, instead of answering from general knowledge.

81
00:05:53,224 --> 00:05:57,590
When an answer is wrong or missing, check that indexing has finished, and

82
00:05:57,590 --> 00:06:00,354
that the passage really contains the answer.

83
00:06:01,104 --> 00:06:05,862
Then try a lower Strictness or more Retrieved documents, and tell the assistant

84
00:06:05,862 --> 00:06:10,004
in its System instructions to answer only from the provided content.

85
00:06:14,204 --> 00:06:15,029
Support:

86
00:06:15,029 --> 00:06:20,274
an assistant answers from your policies and help articles, and links to the source.

87
00:06:21,024 --> 00:06:21,826
Sales:

88
00:06:21,826 --> 00:06:27,244
a price list or a product sheet is one upload away from every conversation.

89
00:06:27,994 --> 00:06:28,795
Staff:

90
00:06:28,795 --> 00:06:33,804
a handbook assistant answers questions about leave, travel and tools.

91
00:06:34,554 --> 00:06:35,334
Review:

92
00:06:35,334 --> 00:06:41,034
with data sources, people check the numbered sources of an answer before they rely on it.

93
00:06:43,034 --> 00:06:47,478
Create the index, upload your documents to a profile, and let the assistant

94
00:06:47,478 --> 00:06:49,507
answer from them, with sources.

95
00:06:49,507 --> 00:06:50,934
Thanks for watching.

